From 5cf3b3742b2e17b45d45ed826a8bae77a87fcca3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Christopher A. Williamson" <contact@chrisaw.io>
Date: Sun, 22 Feb 2026 13:49:15 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] Add Unihertz 8849 hardware controls

Add a settings menu for the Unihertz 8849 (Tank) device-specific
hardware, detected via the Agold HAL and FPGA sysfs interface.

Features:
- Warning light with red/blue/green modes (ioctl 310)
- Camping light with off/full/medium/low/flash/SOS modes (ioctl 301)
- Projector enable/disable via ioctl 500 with display sleep/wake
  cycle for clean FPGA initialization
- Projector mode selection (portrait, landscape, landscape inverted)
- Phone display toggle while projecting
- Projector brightness, keystone correction, fan speed
- Per-device focus calibration via motor sweep with +243 ADC offset
- Manual focus adjustment via motor_turn_mode_step
- Projector temperature and laser rangefinder readout
- Display viewport shrinks to 16:9 when projector is active

The calibration sends cmd() with focus values before the projector
ioctl so the motor_routine_thread starts with the correct table.
AoD is temporarily disabled during enable so the display fully
sleeps for FPGA initialization, then restored afterwards.
Sysfs reads use the Agold daemon's readSysFile() with shell fallback
to avoid SELinux denials for system_app context.
